        "id": 172049,
        "name": "UXM266",
        "username": "UXM266",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/{size}/1966_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-13T16:41:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"seesome\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/48/2018_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> seesome:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One of the toughest fights yet and only my 2nd one-shot that wasn't mint.&nbsp; Got it on my 2nd try with 3 heroes incapped and Expat having only 1hp left (she took out mom with a final shot from Pride).The initial blast from the villian turn is one of the nastiest things I've encountered in the game.&nbsp; Ooof!I really wanted to set up a win using Vis Wresting the exploding Wagons from within her cocoon, as that's one of my favorite things in the game, but I just couldn't keep her alive long enough to do it.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>What a fanatstic ending to that! She wanted to be proud of her daughter, and she thought her mother was to full into her godhood. Very poetic.&nbsp;</p>",
