      {
        "id": 172053,
        "name": "JimmyTheCannon",
        "username": "JimmyTheCannon",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/cdc98d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-18T01:16:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>That was a very close Near Mint. Finished with Fixer at 1 HP and everyone else incapped (so yay, achievement!) It would've been a Mint but I rewound when I accidentally played a style from Fixer's hand that I hadn't meant to play. :-(</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I've never fought Dawn before, and I misremembered her card a round into it. I thought she'd flip at 3 citizens in the trash, so I was careful to only kill 2 initially, then was surprised when she didn't flip after the environment killed a third.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>When she *did* flip and got 2 Citizens out (because Return with the Dawn was in play), I mistakenly left it in instead of destroying it with Visionary's incap power because I forgot she counts as a citizen and she was going to flip back next turn anyways.</p><p>The Explosives Wagon was brutal; it kept me from redirecting with Fixer (right after I played that style with him as the highest HP hero), and I had Imbued Fire out when it exploded with no Flesh of the Sun God, so it did a lot of damage. The second one scared the crap out of me; by that point Fixer was at 7 and Ra and Expat were lower, so if I took it out everyone but Fix would die and he'd be at 1, so I had to leave it alone. This was the first game I got to use Expat's Hairtrigger Reflexes, which ended up taking out the Stout Barrel the turn that it and one of the Hayes brothers came into play, but otherwise it didn't do anything. Then Mr. Hayes casually took out Expat and Ra because they were the 2 lowest non-environment targets (1 and 3, I believe).</p><p>I thought I was screwed, but Dawn ended her turn at 12 HP with Mr. Fixer at exactly 1, with Ra and Expat giving him a power use each for 3 total Bitter Strikes at 4 damage each thanks to the Wagon. Extremely, extremely close.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
